; runner: passive wanderer. drifts forward through memory, looping back when
; the program counter wraps, hoping nobody has dropped a halt in its path.
;
; the noop slide is the whole strategy. after the eighth noop, the program
; counter is incremented one more time and we fall off the end of our own
; instructions. memory is mostly zeros (= noop encoding), so we keep drifting,
; eventually wrapping the address space and ticking back into our own slide.
;
; runner makes no attempt to attack. wins by outlasting opponents that halt
; themselves; loses to anyone (e.g. bomber) writing halts into the memory it
; eventually reads.

